TITLE:: NPVoicerSwitcher
summary:: Manages a pool of NPVoicer objects with atomic swap between current, saved, and released roles
categories:: Control, Live Coding
related:: Classes/Ndef

DESCRIPTION::

NPVoicerSwitcher maintains a pool of link::Classes/NPVoicer:: objects organised into three roles:

list::
## strong::current:: — one active voicer that receives new notes and parameter changes.
## strong::saved:: — an array of code::numSaves:: voicers that have been stepped down from the current role and are still audible.
## strong::released:: — an array of code::numSaves:: voicers that are fading out (or silent), ready to be recycled.
::

The core operation is link::#-swapCurrentToSaved::, which rotates the three roles atomically: 
the current voicer moves to the chosen saved slot, the previous saved voicer begins fading out and moves to the matching released slot, 
and the previous released voicer becomes the new current.

All link::Classes/Ndef:: proxies are created automatically in link::#*new:: and are named with an optional prefix followed by an index starting at 0.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Create a new NPVoicerSwitcher.

argument:: numSaves
Number of saved (and released) voicer slots. Default: code::3::.

argument:: voicerClass
The voicer class to instantiate for each slot. Default: code::NPVoicer::.

argument:: prefix
A link::Classes/String:: prepended to the link::Classes/Ndef:: name of each internal voicer proxy. Default: code::""::.

returns:: An NPVoicerSwitcher instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: current
returns:: The voicer currently in the active role.

METHOD:: saved
returns:: An link::Classes/Array:: of code::numSaves:: voicers in the saved role.

METHOD:: released
returns:: An link::Classes/Array:: of code::numSaves:: voicers in the released (fading-out) role.

METHOD:: allVoicers
returns:: All managed voicers as a flat link::Classes/Array::: code::[current] ++ saved ++ released::.

METHOD:: swapAction
A link::Classes/Function:: that is called after every successful link::#-swapCurrentToSaved:: call. The switcher and the index of the saved slot involved in the swap are passed as arguments. Default: code::nil::.

code::
a.swapAction = { |sw, idx| 
    "Swapped current to saved slot %".format(idx).postln;
};
::

METHOD:: swapCurrentToSaved
Atomically rotate the three roles for a given slot index.

Steps performed:
numberedlist::
## Call code::releaseAll(fadeTime):: on the voicer currently in code::saved[idx]::.
## Move that voicer to code::released[idx]::.
## Move the current voicer to code::saved[idx]::.
## Promote the voicer previously in code::released[idx]:: to current.
## Call link::#-swapAction::.
::

argument:: idx
Zero-based index into the saved/released arrays (code::0 :: to code::numSaves - 1::).

argument:: fadeTime
Fade duration in seconds applied when releasing the outgoing saved voicer. Default: code::5::.

returns:: The receiver.


SUBSECTION:: Sound-related methods

METHOD:: prime
Load a sound definition into the voicers. The call is forwarded to link::Classes/NPVoicer#-prime::.

argument:: obj
The sound object to prime (e.g. a SynthDef name symbol).

argument:: useSpawn
Boolean — passed through to code::NPVoicer::. Default: code::false::.

argument:: which
Optional symbol restricting which role receives the prime call:
list::
## code::nil:: (default) — prime all voicers.
## code::\current:: — prime only the current voicer.
## code::\saved:: — prime only the saved voicers.
## code::\released:: — prime only the released voicers.
::



METHOD:: play
Forward a code::play:: call to every managed voicer.

argument:: outs
Output bus number or link::Classes/Array:: of bus numbers (wrapped if shorter than the voicer count).

argument:: numChannels
Passed through to code::NPVoicer::. Default: code::nil::.

argument:: group
Passed through to code::NPVoicer::. Default: code::nil::.

argument:: multi
Passed through to code::NPVoicer::. Default: code::false::.

argument:: vol
Passed through to code::NPVoicer::. Default: code::nil::.

argument:: fadeTime
Passed through to code::NPVoicer::. Default: code::nil::.

argument:: addAction
Passed through to code::NPVoicer::. Default: code::nil::.

METHOD:: stop
Call code::stop(fadeTime):: on every managed voicer.

argument:: fadeTime
Fade duration in seconds. Default: code::5::.

METHOD:: releaseAll
Call code::releaseAll(fadeTime):: on every managed voicer.

argument:: fadeTime
Fade duration in seconds. Default: code::5::.


SUBSECTION:: Utility methods


METHOD:: numSaves
returns:: The number of saved (and released) slots.

METHOD:: voicerClass
returns:: The voicer class used when creating internal voicer objects.

METHOD:: prefix
returns:: The string prefix used for internal link::Classes/Ndef:: names.


EXAMPLES::

All examples assume the following setup:

code::
(
// SynthDef used by all voicers
SynthDef(\subtractive, { |out = 0, freq = 440, lpFreq = 1000, amp = 0.1, pan = 0, gate = 1|
    var sig  = RLPF.ar(Pulse.ar(freq), lpFreq, 0.1);
    var env  = Env.asr(0.01, 1, 0.1).kr(doneAction: 2, gate: gate);
	
	sig = sig * env * amp;
	sig = Pan2.ar(sig, pan);
    Out.ar(out, sig);
}).add;
)

// Create the switcher: 1 current + 3 saved + 3 released slots (7 voicers total)
q = ();
q.sw = NPVoicerSwitcher(3, NPVoicer);

// Prime all slots with the same SynthDef and start monitoring
q.sw.prime(\subtractive);
q.sw.play;
::

subsection:: first swap

code::
// Play a note on the current voicer
q.sw.current.put(48, [\freq, 48.midicps]);

// normal setting of local parameters...
q.sw.current.setAt(48, \pan, -0.5);
q.sw.current.setAt(48, \pan, 0.5);

// ... as well as global parameters
q.sw.current.set(\lpFreq, 500);


// Swap: current -> saved[2], old saved[2] fades out -> released[2],
//       old released[2] becomes the new current
q.sw.swapCurrentToSaved(2, fadeTime: 2);

// add a note to new current with same ID 
// global parameter set before does not affect it
q.sw.current.put(48, [\freq, 48.midicps]);


// Set lpFreq globally on current voicer...
q.sw.current.set(\lpFreq, 4250)


// ... local setting only affects current voicer
q.sw.current.setAt(48, \pan, -0.5);
q.sw.current.setAt(48, \freq, 48.midicps - 0.2); // slight freq offset
::

subsection:: Using swapAction to print current settings of swapped voicers


code::
q.sw.swapAction = { |sw, idx|
    var currentLpFreq = sw.current.proxy.get(\lpFreq);
    var savedLpFreq = sw.saved[idx].proxy.get(\lpFreq);
    "Swapped current to saved slot %".format(idx).postln;
    "  New current lpFreq: %".format(currentLpFreq).postln;
    "  New saved[%] lpFreq: %".format(idx, savedLpFreq).postln;
};

q.sw.swapCurrentToSaved(0, fadeTime: 3);


q.sw.current.set(\lpFreq, 5000);
q.sw.swapCurrentToSaved(1, fadeTime: 3);
::

subsection:: Inspect the voicer pool

code::
q.sw.allVoicers.do { |v| v.proxy.postln };

q.sw.current.postln;
q.sw.saved.postln;
q.sw.released.postln;
::

subsection:: Clean up

code::
q.sw.releaseAll(fadeTime: 4);
q.sw.stop;
::
